  "analytic_review_groups": [
    "The Gauduchon first mixed-mass bound and local CLN estimate give degree j-1 growth; cancellation of the exact top power improves the total degree to max(n-2,0).",
    "The one-level buffer in truncation preserves locality on the closed finite-depth set; rescaling gives the stated capacity test and bound.",
    "The bounded convex chain rule gives a positive exponential transform, extended to unbounded potentials by decreasing bounded transforms and locality.",
    "Rescaling the bounded exponential transform supplies both polynomial-in-p inverse mass bounds and the explicit capacity constant.",
    "Tonelli for a positive decreasing C1 weight gives total and tail bounds with B_w; finite B_w yields uniform capacity absolute continuity.",
    "The cutoff vanishes at the truncation level, and bounded weighted capacity continuity plus uniform tail control give weak continuity.",
    "Polynomial capacity exponents follow by balancing both terms, with separate zero and large capacity cases; logarithmic endpoint weights retain a>1.",
    "Rescaled infinite-mass witnesses converge in capacity while all stated damping weights converge to the smooth background measure.",
    "Uniform undamped tails first bound total masses, then give a finite limit and weak convergence through bounded cutoffs.",
    "Increasing unbounded integrability weights force tails to vanish; conversely locally finite continuous ramps and Tonelli construct such a weight.",
    "The projective-line truncations have unit mass on shrinking disks and depth exactly j; damping removes their polar limit mass.",
    "Shrinking smooth prescribed-mass potentials converge in capacity; the near-background lower bound and the p-down-to-zero argument give shallow total-variation convergence.",
    "A single weakly convergent subsequence carries the full excess measure for every fixed positive depth, by subtraction of the shallow limits.",
    "The positive expansion bounds every intermediate coefficient; H_j tends to zero in trace norm and dH_j=s_j dh yields closed limits.",
    "Exact and dd-c exact test identities force all claimed vanishing pairings and K_n=0; positivity also gives K_1=0.",
    "The defect decomposition and positive test forms give support restrictions; the pluriclosed extension is retained only in dimension three.",
    "For arbitrary smooth backgrounds a larger Hermitian form gives bounds, while signed local expansion supplies cutoff continuity; tail criteria retain their own uniform-tail hypothesis."
